 "text": "9/29/26, 9:39 AM\nmove-out are further processed.\n\nFeatures\n\nWhen you create a move-out, the system proposes an existing meter reading result for all the billing-relevant registers allocated to\nthe installation for billing purposes. Ensure you have configured the system accordingly in Customizing under |)}*SAP Utilities\nDevice Management Meter Reading Basic Settings Define Control Parameters for Meter Reading Data Processing\n\ne Ifthe system proposes a meter reading result then choose one of the following two options:\no If you adopt the meter reading result, the system adds the meter reading reason End to the result.\no If you change the meter reading result, a new result is created with the meter reading reason End.\n\ne Ifthe system does not propose a meter reading result, you can have it estimate a result or enter one manually. In both\ncases, the system creates a new result with the meter reading reason Move-in.\n\ne If aresult is not created by your adopting/changing a proposed result, and if you do not enter one manually, the system\ncreates a service notification or service order for the register. For more information see service notifications and orders.\n\nAutomatic Estimation of Meter Reading Results During Move-Out\n\nIf a contract is terminated when a supply scenario is created or changed, you can have missing meter readings estimated\nautomatically when you create the move-out.\n\nIf you want to use this function, create an implementation for method STOP_CONTRACT of business add-in (BAdI)\nISU_IDE_DRGSCEN_GEN.\n\nFor more information, see the documentation for the BAdI.\n\nIf you want to use the function for automatically estimating missing meter readings during move-out in the master data generator,\nadjust your master data templates as follows in Customizing for SAP Utilities under |)sCustomer Service \u00bb Master Data\nGenerator Define Master Data Template\n\nAttribute ESTIMATE_MR (Master data generator: Estimate MR Results During Move-Out) must contain the value \"X in all nodes\nof the master data template category MOVE_OUT (Move-Out in Connection with CRM).\n\nMove-Out Reversal\n\nUse\n\nYou use this function to reverse the termination of a contract during move-out. In doing this, the move-out date is set back in the\ncontract. You require this function in the following instances:\n\ne The move-out was mistakenly created with the wrong business partner or with the wrong contract.\n\ne Achanged move-out date subsequently becomes known. In this case, the move-out must be recreated using the changed\nmove-out date after the move-out reversal is performed.\n\ne The move-out only relates to some of the contracts of the business partner. In this case, the move-out must be recreated\nfor the contracts that are actually concerned after the move-out reversal is performed.\n",
